1
00:01:31,319 --> 00:01:32,400
Professor Fang.

2
00:01:35,079 --> 00:01:36,760
Don't jump!

3
00:01:40,879 --> 00:01:41,959
Boss, bosses...

4
00:01:45,519 --> 00:01:47,280
Let me, let me, let me say a few words.

5
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,560
Okay, okay, okay.

6
00:01:52,719 --> 00:01:54,840
Who the hell are you, kid?

7
00:01:55,439 --> 00:01:56,239
Bie Fan.

8
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:59,079
"Don't be annoying"? How can I not be annoyed?!

9
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,079
Do you know how much I...

10
00:02:00,079 --> 00:02:01,599
how much I prepared for today?

11
00:02:01,719 --> 00:02:02,640
I was so close to making it.

12
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:03,959
And you ruined it all!

13
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,719
Why are you being so loud?

14
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,400
My name is Bie Fan.

15
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:10,479
I'm a fan of his.

16
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,680
The three elements of success are:

17
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:13,919
persistence...

18
00:02:14,159 --> 00:02:15,800
Alright, stop reciting.

19
00:02:17,319 --> 00:02:19,719
My mom and I met you together.

20
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:23,159
Do you remember?

21
00:02:23,159 --> 00:02:24,080
Professor Fang.

22
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,840
Do you remember my mom?

23
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:30,560
Buddy,

24
00:02:31,439 --> 00:02:32,360
are... are you...

25
00:02:33,439 --> 00:02:35,000
you know, a little...

26
00:02:39,759 --> 00:02:40,599
like, different from...

27
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:42,879
other people?

28
00:02:44,479 --> 00:02:45,400
Like, really...

29
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:47,000
Do you know what I mean?

30
00:02:48,879 --> 00:02:49,639
This child,

31
00:02:49,639 --> 00:02:51,479
compared to other kids,

32
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:52,680
is very, very...

33
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:55,759
Doctor!

34
00:02:55,759 --> 00:02:56,439
Why... why is...

35
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,240
why is this child's head at the bottom?

36
00:02:58,479 --> 00:02:59,520
You're holding him upside down.

37
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,039
What's his name?

38
00:03:05,039 --> 00:03:06,840
Bie Fan. Didn't you name him?

39
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,039
Right, right, right. This is my son.

40
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,840
My mom said,

41
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,439
other babies cry when they're born,

42
00:03:15,639 --> 00:03:16,400
but you're laughing.

43
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,759
I cried a lot.

44
00:03:23,439 --> 00:03:26,000
You don't need to start from that far back.

45
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:28,000
Actually, I... I mostly want to know...

46
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:31,039
when... when did you start...

47
00:03:31,039 --> 00:03:32,879
perusing my work?

48
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,080
Do you know the word "peruse"? See? See? See?

49
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:35,840
Peruse...

50
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,680
See what? That year, I was born.

51
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:39,719
Born?

52
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,520
My book wasn't even out when you were born!

53
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,080
I'm having an academic discussion here.

54
00:03:44,479 --> 00:03:46,120
Don't keep interrupting me.

55
00:03:49,599 --> 00:03:51,800
What is Success?, page 19:

56
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:54,159
"Success must have a beginning and an end."

57
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,840
Regarding when I

58
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:58,360
started perusing Professor Fang's work,

59
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,319
I must start from the beginning.

60
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,120
When I was three years old,

61
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:09,400
I was the fastest kid in class at solving Tangrams.

62
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:11,800
This kid, Bie Fan,

63
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,039
is just too special.

64
00:04:13,159 --> 00:04:13,960
A genius!

65
00:04:14,199 --> 00:04:16,399
Later, I went to elementary school.

66
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:19,199
This kid is good at solving the Tangram,

67
00:04:19,199 --> 00:04:20,439
but he can't just solve it

68
00:04:20,439 --> 00:04:21,839
from first grade all the way to sixth grade.

69
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:24,040
He's played with that Tangram so much it's got a patina.

70
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:25,199
If your child still

71
00:04:25,199 --> 00:04:26,199
only knows how to solve the Tangram,

72
00:04:26,199 --> 00:04:27,240
then that's really weird.

73
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:30,759
Later, my dad took me to get my IQ tested.

74
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,839
Einstein's IQ

75
00:04:32,959 --> 00:04:33,759
is here.

76
00:04:34,759 --> 00:04:36,720
An average kid's IQ is here.

77
00:04:36,879 --> 00:04:38,399
Your child's IQ

78
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:39,720
is here.

79
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,399
In other words,

80
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,439
your child

81
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:50,839
is half an Einstein.

82
00:04:51,839 --> 00:04:52,439
Why don't you

83
00:04:53,079 --> 00:04:54,079
get tested too?

84
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,079
So what if they're both 78?

85
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,519
Aren't I living just fine?

86
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,600
Your dad.

87
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:09,759
His name just wasn't good.

88
00:05:10,279 --> 00:05:11,360
He was named Bie Yongsheng.

89
00:05:12,519 --> 00:05:14,040
Then, later on...

90
00:05:14,519 --> 00:05:18,399
Because I lost a fight with a classmate at school.

91
00:05:18,439 --> 00:05:18,839
Stop right there!

92
00:05:18,839 --> 00:05:21,439
My mom came to our school.

93
00:05:21,439 --> 00:05:22,160
to sell box lunches.

94
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,959
From now on, I'll be selling box lunches here.

95
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:25,879
If anyone bullies my son again,

96
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,720
I'll chop their hands off!

97
00:05:28,519 --> 00:05:29,439
You hear me?

98
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:30,600
Yes, ma'am.

99
00:05:31,279 --> 00:05:33,680
And then, even later on...

100
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,120
My good friend, Rong Sihai,

101
00:05:36,279 --> 00:05:38,519
gave me a secret martial arts manual.

102
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,759
While I was practicing moves in class,

103
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,920
the professor caught me.

104
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:42,639
Bie Fan!

105
00:05:43,399 --> 00:05:44,040
Bie Fan!

106
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,680
We're about to prep for the college entrance exam!

107
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,519
What are you doing all day...

108
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,759
Come here, squat down for me.

109
00:05:51,199 --> 00:05:54,000
While being scolded by the professor in the office,

110
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,199
I saw Professor Fang's book.

111
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,360
Just read this.

112
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,720
It's still better than reading about this condor!

113
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,120
Your... your professor...

114
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,040
really thinks like this?

115
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,000
Don't interrupt.

116
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,680
Can you let me finish?

117
00:06:05,079 --> 00:06:06,120
Don't interrupt.

118
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,319
Let the kid finish speaking.

119
00:06:09,519 --> 00:06:10,839
You've had it hard since you were little.

120
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:11,920
Always getting bullied.

121
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,720
And didn't have many friends.

122
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,199
Ever since you read Professor Book's Fang...

123
00:06:16,199 --> 00:06:17,920
F- Professor Fang's book,

124
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,759
your life started to change, right?

125
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,959
I wasn't interrupting.

126
00:06:21,199 --> 00:06:22,839
Let me finish what I was saying.

127
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,959
I've been bullied since I was little,

128
00:06:25,199 --> 00:06:26,519
and had hardly any friends.

129
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:29,560
It was after reading Professor Book's Fang...

130
00:06:30,279 --> 00:06:31,399
Fang... Old Fang...

131
00:06:33,279 --> 00:06:34,920
after Professor Book's Fang...

132
00:06:35,199 --> 00:06:37,519
that my life began to change.

133
00:06:37,759 --> 00:06:39,600
Mom, the professor said

134
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,680
the two of us aren't cut out for regular high school.

135
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:43,800
Then what are you cut out for?

136
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,279
Cut out for entering the workforce early.

137
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:47,160
Food, boss!

138
00:06:47,399 --> 00:06:47,879
Coming!

139
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,759
Food's ready, food's ready!

140
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:54,240
Bie Fan, look at how busy your mom is every day.

141
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,639
Thanks! You don't even offer to help her.

142
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,519
How can I help her?

143
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
You could learn to be a chef,

144
00:07:02,279 --> 00:07:03,519
and help her cook and stuff.

145
00:07:10,399 --> 00:07:11,920
So I'll learn to be a chef,

146
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,160
and help her cook.

147
00:07:14,279 --> 00:07:15,680
Then what do you want to do in the future?

148
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,399
I'm going to test into Tsinghua!

149
00:07:21,519 --> 00:07:22,519
What's Tsinghua?

150
00:07:27,319 --> 00:07:29,480
Page 69 of What is Success?,

151
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:30,759
Perseverance.

152
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,720
Perseverance is also an essential virtue for success.

153
00:07:50,199 --> 00:07:50,959
Genius.

154
00:07:53,399 --> 00:07:54,399
Done. Good.

155
00:07:58,879 --> 00:07:59,959
A genius!

156
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,720
The author of What is Success?

157
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,079
actually replied to me!

158
00:08:08,079 --> 00:08:08,920
Sihai.

159
00:08:09,399 --> 00:08:10,199
Look.

160
00:08:10,399 --> 00:08:11,959
Writer Haowen says,

161
00:08:12,079 --> 00:08:13,519
"Keep it up!"

162
00:08:17,279 --> 00:08:18,399
You finally finished reading it.

163
00:08:19,959 --> 00:08:21,399
I memorized the whole thing.

164
00:08:23,279 --> 00:08:24,399
Last page, third sentence.

165
00:08:24,959 --> 00:08:28,160
"Life isn't always what it seems.

166
00:08:28,279 --> 00:08:32,039
You must brave the wind and rain step by step,

167
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:34,159
taste all the bitterness of the world,

168
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:37,039
to realize impermanence is the only constant."

169
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:38,600
Page five, ninth sentence.

170
00:08:38,879 --> 00:08:41,799
"Success is having the power of speech,

171
00:08:41,799 --> 00:08:44,519
while being willing to let others hear your voice."

172
00:08:44,639 --> 00:08:46,279
Page 50, sentence 24.

173
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:49,039
"Success is breathing fresh air.

174
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:52,600
Whether you're in a city office building

175
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,960
or on a stock exchange floor,

176
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:56,840
the air you breathe deeply

177
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,519
will always be refreshing."

178
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:02,720
This carving is really great!

179
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,120
I announce,

180
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:15,960
the winner of this King of Chefs Championship is Bie Fan!

181
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:19,639
And then you succeeded.

182
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,240
No, my success isn't because of the award,

183
00:09:24,559 --> 00:09:25,600
but because of

184
00:09:26,039 --> 00:09:28,200
your validation, Professor Fang.

185
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:39,840
Didn't bring it.

186
00:09:45,279 --> 00:09:46,399
I think I did.

187
00:09:51,679 --> 00:09:53,200
Do you... Do you want me to help you find it?

188
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:55,559
Professor Fang, don't touch my things.

189
00:09:55,559 --> 00:09:56,200
Okay?

190
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:04,159
Is... Is this...

191
00:10:04,559 --> 00:10:05,840
Isn't this that Nine-Turn...

192
00:10:06,519 --> 00:10:07,360
I'm not tasting it.

193
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:09,679
You even ate one back then.

194
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,200
I succeeded.

195
00:10:11,759 --> 00:10:12,399
Mom.

196
00:10:12,399 --> 00:10:15,279
The darkest period of my life,

197
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,440
I relied on Professor Fang's book

198
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,559
to keep me going.

199
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:25,679
Mom?

200
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,000
Are you done pooping?

201
00:10:30,639 --> 00:10:31,320
Mom?

202
00:10:32,159 --> 00:10:33,440
Are you done pooping or what?

203
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,519
What's wrong?

204
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:35,960
Mom! Sis, are you okay?

205
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,399
Hello, is this 120?

206
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:49,600
Son,

207
00:10:49,759 --> 00:10:51,639
go buy me a sugary drink.

208
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,200
Mom might have low blood sugar.

209
00:10:54,639 --> 00:10:55,399
Hurry up.

210
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:56,399
Go buy it.

211
00:10:59,879 --> 00:11:01,639
Lung cancer. Terminal stage.

212
00:11:04,679 --> 00:11:05,240
No way.

213
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,639
I don't even smoke.

214
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,120
Is it curable?

215
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,000
Hard to say.

216
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,600
It depends on how the surgery goes.

217
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:14,759
How much will it cost?

218
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:15,480
About 200,000.

219
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,440
What?

220
00:11:18,399 --> 00:11:20,080
Did you look at the balance on my bank card

221
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:20,879
when you said that?

222
00:11:21,399 --> 00:11:24,000
Mom, Uncle Zhang down the street said

223
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,759
these all cure low blood sugar.

224
00:11:26,799 --> 00:11:27,799
Cure low blood sugar?

225
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,879
That little shop of your Uncle Zhang's

226
00:11:33,879 --> 00:11:34,960
will go out of business sooner or later.

227
00:11:35,519 --> 00:11:36,320
Son,

228
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,879
Mom needs to be hospitalized for checkups.

229
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,279
Take good care of yourself at home.

230
00:11:43,559 --> 00:11:45,600
I made you dumplings and froze them in the fridge.

231
00:11:45,919 --> 00:11:46,919
Boil some yourself when you're hungry.

232
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,240
And your change of clothes,

233
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,679
I've laid them all out on the bed for you.

234
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,039
Take off your dirty clothes

235
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,000
and leave them there.

236
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,679
Mom will wash them for you when I get back, okay?

237
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:58,759
Stop fussing with that.

238
00:11:59,279 --> 00:12:01,279
There are doctors and nurses here.

239
00:12:01,279 --> 00:12:03,639
Hurry, go to school.

240
00:12:05,919 --> 00:12:07,679
I... I don't want to go to school.

241
00:12:08,679 --> 00:12:10,879
You don't want to go? What do you want to do?

242
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,519
When I went to school before,

243
00:12:14,559 --> 00:12:16,679
Mom sold box lunches at the gate to stay with me.

244
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,159
Now I want to stay downstairs

245
00:12:18,159 --> 00:12:19,399
and sell box lunches to stay with Mom.

246
00:12:22,399 --> 00:12:24,039
You have to go to school.

247
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,360
Selling box lunches is a dead end.

248
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,279
Do you hear me?

249
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:32,080
You need to study hard.

250
00:12:37,519 --> 00:12:39,480
"What is Success?", page 34:

251
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:42,279
Success is not defined by others,

252
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,679
but living out your own meaning.

253
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,799
What disease did Auntie say she has?

254
00:12:56,759 --> 00:12:59,679
My mom said she has low blood sugar.

255
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,320
And then?

256
00:13:11,559 --> 00:13:12,519
Did your mom get better?

257
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,879
Later, my mom passed away.

258
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,080
I'm not cooking! I'm not cooking!

259
00:13:41,639 --> 00:13:42,120
Let me pour you a drink.

260
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,759
No, no, let me. I'm the junior here.

261
00:13:46,159 --> 00:13:47,159
Hello, everyone.

262
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,759
I'm Gao Guilan.

263
00:13:50,759 --> 00:13:52,000
The one cooking right now...

264
00:13:52,399 --> 00:13:54,559
must be my son, Bie Fan.

265
00:13:57,039 --> 00:13:58,360
I told you I shouldn't cook!

266
00:14:00,919 --> 00:14:01,720
Today,

267
00:14:01,879 --> 00:14:04,360
I don't know how many friends and family came to see me off,

268
00:14:05,559 --> 00:14:06,639
but I know

269
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:10,519
my son might not be the best host.

270
00:14:12,279 --> 00:14:14,360
I hope you can all forgive him.

271
00:14:15,159 --> 00:14:17,240
He is a very special child,

272
00:14:17,759 --> 00:14:20,320
but he's warm, devoted,

273
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:23,039
kind, and honest.

274
00:14:23,679 --> 00:14:26,279
I also hope every guest here

275
00:14:26,759 --> 00:14:28,159
won't be too sad.

276
00:14:28,759 --> 00:14:31,000
Birth, aging, illness, and death are inevitable.

277
00:14:31,639 --> 00:14:36,919
Lastly, I hope you all eat and drink well.

278
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,960
And I also beg you all,

279
00:14:40,559 --> 00:14:42,159
in the days to come,

280
00:14:43,279 --> 00:14:45,159
to be kind to my son.

281
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,759
Thank you all.

282
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,159
Bie Fan,

283
